IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Red Cross Society Act 1973 (Singapore) -- who may use the red cross emblem and the words "Red Cross" or "Geneva Cross",
-- and the offence (s 10); where the Society's income and property may go (s 12); who is a member (s 3); the Chairperson's term,
-- revocation, resignation and the unexpired-term replacement (ss 7, 8); the Council's rule-making, which needs the approval of the
-- Director-General of Health (s 9(2)); and the grounds of distinction the Society's objects rule out (s 5).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/5/2023"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SRCSA1973.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021";
-- the latest amendment annotated is "Act 11 of 2023 wef 01/05/2023" against s 9(2). Section 10 carries the annotation [55/2007].
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0214 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. For an ordinary person or business the answer is mostly s 10: the emblem and the two phrases are reserved,
-- on pain of a fine up to $10,000 and 6 months. Not encoded: s 1 (short title), s 2 (definitions, used in the names here), s 4 (the
-- Geneva Conventions recognition), s 6 (the President as patron), s 9(1) (the Council's general powers), and s 11 (the 1973 transfer
-- of the Association's property, liabilities and staff). The Society's own rules and any Ministerial authorisations were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Red Cross Society Act 1973`

§§ `10 -- use of the "Red Cross"`

-- s 10(1): "No person other than the Society and any person so authorised by the Minister may use -- (a) the heraldic emblem of the
-- red cross on a white ground formed by reversing the Federal Colours of Switzerland; or (b) the words "Red Cross" or "Geneva Cross"."
-- (2): a contravention is an offence, "liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 6 months or to both".
--
-- The text states no mental element, no exception for prior or good-faith use, and no exception for a translation or a similar
-- device. The red crescent, the red crystal and a green (pharmacy) cross are not named in s 10; whether other law protects them was
-- not looked at (inference from silence, not a reading of any other Act).
DECLARE Mark IS ONE OF
    `a red cross on a white ground`
    `the words Red Cross`
    `the words Geneva Cross`
    `a red crescent`
    `a green cross`
    `a white cross on a red ground`

GIVEN `the mark` IS A Mark
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mark is reserved by s 10` IF
    CONSIDER `the mark`
    WHEN `a red cross on a white ground` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the words Red Cross` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the words Geneva Cross` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the mark` IS A Mark, `the user is the Society` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is an offence under s 10` IF
    `the mark is reserved by s 10` `the mark` AND (NOT `the user is the Society`) AND (NOT `authorised by the Minister`)

GIVEN `fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER, `months of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sentence is within the s 10 maximum` IF
    `fine in dollars` AT MOST 10000 AND `months of imprisonment` AT MOST 6

§§ `12 -- application of income and property`

-- s 12: income and property "must be applied solely towards the promotion of the objects of the Society ... and no part thereof may
-- be paid or transferred directly or indirectly by way of dividend, bonus or otherwise by way of profit to the members of the
-- Society". Proviso: nothing precludes "the payment in good faith of remuneration to any officer or employee of the Society or to any
-- member of the Society in return for services rendered to the Society".
DECLARE Payment IS ONE OF
    `spending on relief within the objects`
    `a dividend to members`
    `a bonus to members`
    `a distribution of surplus to members`
    `remuneration for services rendered`

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment, `made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment is permitted by s 12` IF
    CONSIDER `the payment`
    WHEN `spending on relief within the objects` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `remuneration for services rendered` THEN `made in good faith`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 -- membership`

-- s 3(3): "The Society consists of all persons who immediately before 6 April 1973 were members of the Association and all such
-- persons as may, after that date, become members of the Society pursuant to the rules for the time being in force of the Society."
-- Whether and how membership ends is left to the rules; this encoding does not model it.
GIVEN `a member of the Association immediately before 6 April 1973` IS A BOOLEAN, `admitted under the Society's rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a member of the Society` IF
    `a member of the Association immediately before 6 April 1973` OR `admitted under the Society's rules`

§§ `7, 8 -- the Chairperson`

-- s 7(2): the Chairperson "must be appointed by the President for a term of 3 years, and is eligible for re-appointment".
-- s 8(1): the President "may at any time revoke the appointment ... if the President considers it desirable in the interests of the
-- Society". (2): the Chairperson "may by writing addressed to the President resign". (3): if the Chairperson dies, is revoked or
-- otherwise vacates office before the term expires, "another person may be appointed by the President for the unexpired period".
-- The Act says nothing about when a resignation takes effect.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Chairperson's term in months` MEANS 36

GIVEN `the President considers it desirable in the interests of the Society` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the President may revoke the appointment` IF
    `the President considers it desirable in the interests of the Society`

GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `addressed to the President` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resignation is in the form s 8(2) describes` IF
    `in writing` AND `addressed to the President`

GIVEN `months the predecessor served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months a replacement may be appointed for` MEANS
    IF `months the predecessor served` AT LEAST `the Chairperson's term in months` THEN 0
    ELSE `the Chairperson's term in months` MINUS `months the predecessor served`

§§ `9(2) -- the Council's rules`

-- s 9(2): "The Council may, with the approval of the Director-General of Health, make rules for or in respect of" (a) proceedings and
-- management; (b) classes of members and terms of admission; (c) the executive committee and officers; (d) sub-committees and
-- delegation; (e) meetings and voting; (f) accounts and "the audit of the accounts at least once a year"; (g) the annual general
-- meeting. [Act 11 of 2023 wef 01/05/2023]. Whether rules made without approval are void is not said; this reads the approval as a
-- condition of the power (inference).
DECLARE RuleTopic IS ONE OF
    `classes of members and terms of admission`
    `the annual general meeting`
    `keeping and auditing the accounts`
    `the executive committee`
    `a levy on non-members`

GIVEN `the topic` IS A RuleTopic, `approved by the Director-General of Health` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Council may make the rule under s 9(2)` IF
    `approved by the Director-General of Health` AND
        CONSIDER `the topic`
        WHEN `a levy on non-members` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 9(2)(f) speaks of rules for "the audit of the accounts at least once a year". Read as a floor on what such rules provide.
GIVEN `audits each year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the audit frequency meets s 9(2)(f)` IF
    `audits each year` AT LEAST 1

§§ `5 -- objects`

-- s 5(a): assistance in relief operations in disaster and auxiliary health and welfare services "to the sick, the handicapped, the
-- aged and the poor, without any distinction on grounds of race, nationality, religion or political opinions". Only those four
-- grounds are named.
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `race`
    `nationality`
    `religion`
    `political opinions`
    `some other ground`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(a) names the ground` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `some other ground` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
